#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222306} :activity/id #uuid "4bdf9815-fa54-50ce-b3f5-ad6d001dd7d2" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050054 :topic/id #uuid "29ce72ae-dbea-5d83-a81d-90545461cdec" :topic/math-academy-id 6375} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222306 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222473 :tutorial/content "In this topic, we'll learn how to compute the **matrix exponential**.\n\nRecall that the scalar exponential function $e^t$ can be written as the power series \n\n$$\ne^t = \\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}\\dfrac{t^k}{k!} = 1 + t + \\dfrac{t^2}{2} + \\cdots + \\dfrac{t^k}{k!} + \\cdots.\n$$\n\nNow, let $A$ be an $n\\times n$ matrix. By definition, the matrix exponential $e^{At}$ is given by the analogous series\n\n$$\ne^{At} = \\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}\\frac{A^k t^k}{k!} = I + tA + \\dfrac{t^2}{2}A^2 + \\cdots + \\dfrac{t^k}{k!}A^k + \\cdots.\n$$\n\nThere are several approaches for computing matrix exponentials:\n\n- The most direct approach is to use the definition above, but this is typically impractical.\n\n- Another method, often covered in linear algebra courses, is to use the Jordan canonical form of $A$. This works, but it can also be tedious, especially for larger matrices.\n\nHere, we will introduce a different method.\n\nBy the Cayley–Hamilton theorem, every power $A^n, A^{n+1}, \\ldots$ can be rewritten as a linear combination of \n\n$$\nI, \\: A, \\: A^2, \\: \\ldots, \\: A^{n-1}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, $e^{At}$ can be written in the form\n\n$$\ne^{At}=\\alpha_{n-1}A^{n-1} t^{n-1}+\\alpha_{n-2} A^{n-2}t^{n-2}+\\cdots+\\alpha_1 At+\\alpha_0 I,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha_0, \\alpha_1, \\ldots, \\alpha_{n-1}$ are functions of $t$ and $I$ is the $n \\times n$ identity matrix. \n\nNow, we define the polynomial \n\n$$\nr(\\lambda)=\\alpha_{n-1}\\lambda^{n-1}+\\alpha_{n-2}\\lambda^{n-2}+\\cdots+\\alpha_1\\lambda+\\alpha_0.\n$$\n\nThen we have the following key fact:\n\n> For any eigenvalue $\\lambda$ of $At$, we have $r(\\lambda) = e^{\\lambda}.$\n\nLet’s now see how this method works in practice." :tutorial/id #uuid "d78b3664-4117-56fc-bf30-5ca3acb28377" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14270 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "f932ab79-9fa6-5a87-aa94-755b1685c4e3" :step/math-academy-id 588472 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222307}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222307 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222482 :tutorial/content "Let's find $e^{At}$ for <div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div> \n\nBy solving the characteristic polynomial $|A-\\lambda I|=0,$ we can find that the eigenvalues of $A$ are \n\n$$\n\\lambda_1=2, \\qquad\n\\lambda_2=7.\n$$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 7\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 0 \\\\ -7{\\alpha }_{1}t & 7{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_0$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda) = \\alpha_1 \\lambda + \\alpha_0.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n\\lambda_1=2t, \\qquad\n\\lambda_2=7t,\n$$\n\nboth of multiplicity one. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}r(2t) &={e}^{2t} \\\\ r(7t) &={e}^{7t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\Rightarrow \\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{2t} \\\\ 7t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{7t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_0{:}$\n\n- Subtracting the first equation from the second one, we get\n\n$$\n5t\\alpha_1 = e^{7t} - e^{2t}\n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\n\\alpha_1 = \\dfrac{1}{5t}\\bigl(e^{7t}-e^{2t}\\bigr).\n$$\n\n- Multiplying the first equation by $7$ and subtracting twice the second one, we get\n\n$$\n5\\alpha_0 = 7e^{2t} - 2e^{7t}\n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\n\\alpha_0 = \\dfrac{1}{5}\\bigl(7e^{2t}-2e^{7t}\\bigr).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_0$ into the expressions for the entries of $e^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =2(\\frac{1}{5t}({e}^{7t}-{e}^{2t}))t+\\frac{1}{5}(7{e}^{2t}-2{e}^{7t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}((2{e}^{7t}-2{e}^{2t})+(7{e}^{2t}-2{e}^{7t})) \\\\  & ={e}^{2t} \\\\ -7{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-7(\\frac{1}{5t}({e}^{7t}-{e}^{2t}))t \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{5}({e}^{7t}-{e}^{2t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}({e}^{2t}-{e}^{7t}) \\\\ 7{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =7(\\frac{1}{5t}({e}^{7t}-{e}^{2t}))t+\\frac{1}{5}(7{e}^{2t}-2{e}^{7t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}((7{e}^{7t}-7{e}^{2t})+(7{e}^{2t}-2{e}^{7t})) \\\\  & ={e}^{7t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5{e}^{2t} & 0 \\\\ 7({e}^{2t}-{e}^{7t}) & 5{e}^{7t}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "6e5aa695-b237-54d4-9836-20514d70dc9e" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14389 :tutorial/title "2x2 Matrices With Distinct Real Eigenvalues"} :step/id #uuid "3c91134a-154b-5692-a2cc-fdc45c81af7e" :step/math-academy-id 588473 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222308}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222308 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221408 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221150 :question/id #uuid "35a158c3-37b6-5123-ba90-1fd05218ce43" :question/math-academy-id "e-21271"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fee186e0-579f-5104-b0e1-50540abc0bdc" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050001}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221925} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221994} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308532} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308533} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308644} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308645}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Exponent for a Matrix With Distinct Real Eigenvalues"} :step/id #uuid "ebe4cfdc-9e1a-577d-ad38-9d117b4cf820" :step/math-academy-id 588474 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222309}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222309 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221409 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221151 :question/id #uuid "18064c11-63d3-599a-b504-7b589f46c3dc" :question/math-academy-id "e-21272"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a118fe4a-cd1f-52f7-aa33-59f5494e4905" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048305}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221932} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222002} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308654} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308655} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308656} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308657} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308658} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308659} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308660} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370129} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532679}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Exponent for a Matrix With Distinct Complex Eigenvalues"} :step/id #uuid "ea0b2d60-3227-5e25-b6a9-171c0dc66319" :step/math-academy-id 588478 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222310}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222310 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222481 :tutorial/content "Recall that the matrix exponential $e^{At}$ can be written as\n\n$$\ne^{At}=\\alpha_{n-1} A^{n-1}t^{n-1}+\\alpha_{n-2} A^{n-2}t^{n-2}+\\cdots+\\alpha_1 At+\\alpha_0 I.\n$$\n\nIf we define the polynomial\n\n$$\nr(\\lambda)=\\alpha_{n-1}\\lambda^{n-1}+\\alpha_{n-2}\\lambda^{n-2}+\\cdots+\\alpha_1\\lambda+\\alpha_0,\n$$\n\nthen for any eigenvalue $\\lambda_i$ of $At,$ we have\n\n$$\nr(\\lambda_i) = e^{\\lambda_i}.\n$$\n\nHowever, for *repeated eigenvalues*, we have the following additional fact:\n\n> If $\\lambda_i$ is an eigenvalue of multiplicity $k$ with $k>1,$ then \n> \n> \n> $$\n> \\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(\\lambda ){|}_{\\lambda ={\\lambda }_{i}}={e}^{{\\lambda }_{i}},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{\\lambda }^{2}}r(\\lambda ){|}_{\\lambda ={\\lambda }_{i}}={e}^{{\\lambda }_{i}},\\,…,\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{k-1}}{\\text{d}{\\lambda }^{k-1}}r(\\lambda ){|}_{\\lambda ={\\lambda }_{i}}={e}^{{\\lambda }_{i}}\\end{aligned}\n> $$\n\nLet's apply these facts to a concrete example." :tutorial/id #uuid "d7b15b25-b73f-5d5f-aa02-e4c1a5e9804e" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14388 :tutorial/title "2x2 Matrices With Repeated Eigenvalues"} :step/id #uuid "855a741b-2bbe-5e04-b892-8d1d9c7d0e65" :step/math-academy-id 588481 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222311}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222311 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221410 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221152 :question/id #uuid "40a6318a-a1c9-55f3-afdb-02b43891d7b5" :question/math-academy-id "e-21273"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0fd1d280-c768-5504-892e-a9a1948e1f1a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221933} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222003} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308670} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308671} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308672} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308673} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308674} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308675} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370138} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553504} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561040}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Exponent for a Matrix With Repeated Eigenvalues"} :step/id #uuid "de5a7d5c-0c01-5247-8ba6-a69a863c9cbb" :step/math-academy-id 588482 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222312}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222312 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222505 :tutorial/content "Again, let $A$ be a constant $n\\times n$ matrix. The matrix exponential satisfies\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\bigl(e^{At}\\bigr)=A\\,e^{At}.\n$$\n\nIndeed, recall that\n\n$$\ne^{At}=\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}\\frac{(At)^k}{k!}\n=\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}\\frac{A^k t^k}{k!}.\n$$\n\nTo prove the formula, we differentiate the series above term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}) & ={\\sum }_{k=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{A}^{k}\\cdot k{t}^{k-1}}{k!} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{A}^{k}{t}^{k-1}}{(k-1)!} \\\\  & =A{\\sum }_{k=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{A}^{k-1}{t}^{k-1}}{(k-1)!} \\\\  & =A{\\sum }_{j=0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{A}^{j}{t}^{j}}{j!} \\\\  & =A\\,{e}^{At}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "739548ab-310c-5de3-a426-1fcaa3282478" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14526 :tutorial/title "Derivatives of Matrix Exponentials"} :step/id #uuid "fc10fbf4-2be0-5b3f-ad2e-0505b175d5a6" :step/math-academy-id 588485 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222313}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222313 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221411 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221194 :question/id #uuid "c0213c76-94e8-5ab3-a260-8a78a205589a" :question/math-academy-id "e-21724"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4fc3ba4-d488-5156-88dc-837369269cef" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221995} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222006} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308726} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308727} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308728} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308729} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308730} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308731} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308732} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370312} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370321}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Matrix Exponential"} :step/id #uuid "df4956ab-0323-513e-ab21-66734987f4d0" :step/math-academy-id 588486 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222314}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222314 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222506 :tutorial/content "Matrix exponentials have other properties. We list a few of them:\n\n- *Law of Exponents:* If $A$ is a constant square matrix, then\n\n$$\ne^{A(t+s)} = e^{At}\\,e^{As}.\n$$\n\n- *Inverse:* For any $t,$ the matrix $e^{At}$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n(e^{At})^{-1} = e^{-At}.\n$$\n\n- *Identity:* For any square matrix $A,$\n\n$$\ne^{A\\cdot 0} = I.\n$$\n\n- *Product of exponentials:* If $A$ and $B$ commute (i.e., $AB = BA$), then\n\n$$\ne^{A}e^{B} = e^{A+B}.\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** In general, this identity is *not true* unless $A$ and $B$ commute." :tutorial/id #uuid "2fcc3801-5d58-5c8e-b8c8-7be65b34f71a" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14527 :tutorial/title "Properties of the Matrix Exponential"} :step/id #uuid "24b8ab46-a4b1-5358-abbd-db086f102dbf" :step/math-academy-id 588489}] :activity/title "Matrix Exponentials" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186221467}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046645} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532736} :activity/id #uuid "e67bdbbc-b2ac-5dc2-96db-49866bc692da" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050054 :topic/id #uuid "29ce72ae-dbea-5d83-a81d-90545461cdec" :topic/math-academy-id 6375} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532728 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308670 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5a54273-3450-5c26-84d7-383486f21cec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307277}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307277} :answer-field/id #uuid "3db64a2d-0768-5ffd-ba7e-05c9f4485c48" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307712} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec22e530-554e-5020-8783-f257d54f500f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307324}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307324} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5cf4951-3613-5027-8a9a-0372890bd5d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "79079e07-e6bc-5f6a-8ed1-2ff769b8b920" :question/math-academy-id "q-334729" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\n*Hint: The only eigenvalue of $A$ is $3,$ and it has multiplicity two.*\n\n| ${e}^{At}={e}^{3t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $3t$ | $1-3t$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & -3{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 3{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=3t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}r(3t) &={e}^{3t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(3t) &={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{3t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1} &={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{3t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n3t{e}^{3t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{3t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{3t}(1-3t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =6{e}^{3t}t+{e}^{3t}(1-3t) \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}(1+3t), \\\\ -3{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-3{e}^{3t}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{3t}\\begin{bmatrix}1+3t & -3t \\\\ 3t & 1-3t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "03d5d0e2-58f6-580f-b08d-c488e5333a32" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532761}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532736 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532679 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a8db4e8-f732-5d22-9704-09e0ccf298b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\cos(3t)+\\sin(3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532285}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532285} :answer-field/id #uuid "3247c73e-d754-5617-80f3-a0beacefea90" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532515} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f84eb7c6-9806-5d01-aade-ce5ce09883c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\sin(3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532472}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532472} :answer-field/id #uuid "4788b925-6ee1-5536-8ffa-a6478b71d51d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "900adaef-859d-5d14-9981-202d2269e069" :question/math-academy-id "q-334626" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $2\\pm 3\\text{i}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${e}^{At}={e}^{2t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"140px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"140px\">$2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr></tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 6{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -3{\\alpha }_{1}t & -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues or $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=(2+3\\text{i})t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=(2-3\\text{i})t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((2+3\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(2+3\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(2+3\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & ={e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) \\\\ (2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0})+3{\\alpha }_{1}\\text{i}t & ={e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}\\,{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ 3t{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{1}{3t}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t))\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{3t}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\cdot t+{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\frac{2}{3}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) \\\\ -3{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3t}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =-{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "447659a5-783c-55e2-b7bc-7044e79e9190" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532744}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532744 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308657 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7805cc61-032d-5340-b315-43d00f9ec949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}(3t)-\\operatorname{sin}(3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306291}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306291} :answer-field/id #uuid "5694d036-6e3a-56ea-beeb-680490a87b8c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307787} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aacf013a-2689-512b-8794-bcbacddaf843" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{sin}(3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306764}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306764} :answer-field/id #uuid "674d0fa8-85cf-5f7e-bdaa-2d7ca81bb93d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307849}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f29b7109-5c33-5046-8236-7d693dea5b92" :question/math-academy-id "q-334634" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $\\pm 3\\text{i}.$*\n\n| ${e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\,$ |  | $3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$ | $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 2{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -5{\\alpha }_{1}t & -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues or $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=3\\text{i}t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-3\\text{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(3\\text{i}t) & ={e}^{3\\text{i}t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}\\cdot 3\\text{i}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+3{\\alpha }_{1}\\text{i}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ 3{\\alpha }_{1}t &=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1} &=\\frac{1}{3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-\\frac{1}{3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\cdot t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "783d8e6f-d461-5f0b-8f11-aa192fbe52a4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532728}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532761 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308672 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52b1d7ae-e4dd-5799-9115-e6e7b1fd12ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305951}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305951} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dde19ef-9af0-5255-a3d4-655b000140c4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307818} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fc7ea02-06bd-5e6c-aed2-4751d80186b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+6t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305289}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305289} :answer-field/id #uuid "893c4189-3f31-573e-94ae-26b874312a53" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4bf1a0f0-bb87-5dac-ad3b-1ce93c87e2a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-334733" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -3 \\\\ 12 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\n*Hint: The only eigenvalue of $A$ is $2,$ and it has multiplicity two.*\n\n| ${e}^{At}={e}^{2t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $-3t$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $1-6t$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -3 \\\\ 12 & -4\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & -3{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 12{\\alpha }_{1}t & -4{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=2t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}r(2t) &={e}^{2t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(2t) &={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{2t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1} &={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{2t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n2t{e}^{2t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t}(1-2t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =8{e}^{2t}t+{e}^{2t}(1-2t) \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}(1+6t) \\\\ 12{\\alpha }_{1}t & =12{e}^{2t}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}1+6t & -3t \\\\ 12t & 1-6t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "dc3bbe46-b9a2-5b99-9ca0-73318c047651" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532762}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532762 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308729 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "753cf168-9af8-50a8-bf6d-aec9b1e3c2e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7\\operatorname{cos}(7t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306266}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306266} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e34fb24-26d6-54f8-8e2c-e459754da21c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307665} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa9799e7-8c6d-5377-a47d-4e6a05e2b186" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\operatorname{cos}(7t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306762}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306762} :answer-field/id #uuid "4609b934-301d-57c7-89ed-e8cdd2469bcc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307743} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f24e94e-6875-5dc6-95dc-6ad3d893da7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7\\operatorname{sin}(7t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305283}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305283} :answer-field/id #uuid "95f2f7b3-4e91-5fb5-bc50-5086640214d7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307996} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "680c33fd-8ce1-50c7-9c3f-e14b4d6e395c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7\\operatorname{sin}(7t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306145}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306145} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0d0c784-8e29-5661-9d95-8147778f15de" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "14f4f5f9-2f59-5657-8bee-d1931d1011cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-335107" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices $A$ and ${e}^{At}$ above, compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}).$\n\n| $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=A\\,{e}^{At}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}) & =A\\,{e}^{At} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & -7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) \\\\ 7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & -7\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "eabd75d2-306c-5778-a5d4-6908c275c489"}] :activity/title "Matrix Exponentials" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531935}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046669} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553677} :activity/id #uuid "02ab6ed4-47f1-525b-9777-cf24c2343051" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050054 :topic/id #uuid "29ce72ae-dbea-5d83-a81d-90545461cdec" :topic/math-academy-id 6375} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553597 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308730 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e5577e5-b719-5b3f-b68d-1a75b4f32803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{sin}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306635}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306635} :answer-field/id #uuid "44dfc463-2eed-5b8f-a49b-1a3832e8c840" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307736} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0a7c5d9-d376-5bfc-a898-b72ac7a7d83b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{cos}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307230}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307230} :answer-field/id #uuid "53a80531-ea9b-5f87-832d-76058c53931d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307774} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b1ecd54-364c-5cc5-a146-14c0aa79943d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306024}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306024} :answer-field/id #uuid "93f4d138-3d8f-5af5-bab0-3f349b34eb48" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307989} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c31d763-cb9f-53cb-b3d1-d640d1818379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{sin}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305410}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305410} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb057fc7-7654-5c34-bfa6-3eaa85ee1200" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d14a11c3-0a49-5696-a62c-af65df34be1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-335108" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices $A$ and ${e}^{At}$ above, compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}).$\n\n| $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=A\\,{e}^{At}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}) & =A\\,{e}^{At} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & -5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & -5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0b4cefa4-af80-5c7c-83a1-ff4d5ac31dcb"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553601 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370129 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7afe076b-ab10-5a6d-92ee-d9bda36095eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370131}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370131} :answer-field/id #uuid "8717736e-bf1d-56b9-8978-2ee27ddc1c10" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370130} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "116b716d-7743-526a-8367-67bb770fa2aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370133}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370133} :answer-field/id #uuid "6684d3cf-4512-5e44-a922-9538752b4a1d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "eace89bb-5f6d-586f-b6ba-d2d1f4b38da0" :question/math-academy-id "q-334633" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $\\pm \\text{i}.$*\n\n| ${e}^{At}=\\,\\,$ |  | $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\alpha }_{0} & -{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues or $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-\\text{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(\\text{i}t) & ={e}^{\\text{i}t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}\\cdot \\text{i}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+{\\alpha }_{1}\\text{i}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t &=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1} &=\\frac{1}{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-\\frac{1}{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t & =\\frac{1}{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "16872273-54fb-5073-a5e6-85ee3dbf9ea6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553611}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553611 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308674 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cddbd6d-ffb7-5530-be33-109a25cb590f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305736}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305736} :answer-field/id #uuid "28239443-16fd-5045-bb7b-a3e946af529a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307647} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fff644e-a154-526d-b37a-e4f82a475e0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306218}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306218} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cec750e-1b50-5e87-b62d-239edf61a752" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307873}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d74b37d0-1ddd-5304-877c-4617a1e8ae03" :question/math-academy-id "q-334735" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\n*Hint: The only eigenvalue of $A$ is $3,$ and it has multiplicity two.*\n\n| ${e}^{At}={e}^{3t}\\,\\,$ |  | $1+4t$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $8t$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -1\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & -2{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 8{\\alpha }_{1}t & -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=3t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}r(3t) &={e}^{3t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(3t) &={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{3t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1} &={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{3t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n3t{e}^{3t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{3t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{3t}(1-3t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-2{e}^{3t}t \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}(-2t) \\\\ -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-{e}^{3t}t+{e}^{3t}(1-3t) \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}(1-4t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{3t}\\begin{bmatrix}1+4t & -2t \\\\ 8t & 1-4t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "30faf73f-f8c2-56a2-805f-6ce1667a314c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553678}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553677 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221995 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f71d01b6-ee5b-5054-8b30-0826abc684a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(1+2t)e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553358}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553358} :answer-field/id #uuid "9199806a-56d9-516c-b5c9-c3a184f8a0be" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220637} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8adba1a9-ea42-59fb-9093-1e1960d724e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553150}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553150} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfd89e18-df1a-52e5-b1a9-13b9a350e74e" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220638} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79588b6e-67a9-51cd-86b3-3db3fa8e6c66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553116}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553116} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d46c25a-b0e5-5cb8-b4d9-bcfcbeae85f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220639} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4f1d256-cbeb-55b4-a0df-384c213379d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553295}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553295} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c309815-d4c5-5708-9d45-6e7c0e1436e3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220640}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e415201f-e8d7-5cac-99e4-ae2f79b7e01e" :question/math-academy-id "q-333858" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices $A$ and ${e}^{At}$ above, compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}).$\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr></tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=A\\,{e}^{At}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}) & =A\\,{e}^{At} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2t} & (2t+1){e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e0e6cc77-900e-5194-bf84-c2fa20bd1df9" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553601}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553678 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553504 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8abba599-d405-5b28-8292-a43ed4750a5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553149}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553149} :answer-field/id #uuid "03ccd2db-1552-543e-9102-8cfc8d2f158f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553378} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9e4d7af-e293-52fb-87b2-17e379489288" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-8t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553364}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553364} :answer-field/id #uuid "416cdcae-3262-544e-a6bf-81a343fec464" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553403}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "23c462cc-da9f-5356-aacb-68452f1af0c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-334736" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The only eigenvalue of $A$ is $-2,$ and it has multiplicity two.*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${e}^{At}={e}^{-2t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$1-4t$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$1+4t$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 2{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -8{\\alpha }_{1}t & 2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-2t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}r(-2t)={e}^{-2t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(-2t)={e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}(-2t){\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-2t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-2t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n-2t{e}^{-2t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-2t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-2t}(1+2t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\alpha }_{1}t & =2{e}^{-2t}t \\\\  & ={e}^{-2t}(2t) \\\\ -8{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-8{e}^{-2t}t \\\\  & ={e}^{-2t}(-8t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1-4t & 2t \\\\ -8t & 1+4t\\end{aligned}].\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "eb5fe771-6cf7-59f9-a5b4-123061340a58" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553597}}] :activity/title "Matrix Exponentials" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552851}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046669} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561082} :activity/id #uuid "73992d71-b996-5316-ad0f-63db7204241f" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050054 :topic/id #uuid "29ce72ae-dbea-5d83-a81d-90545461cdec" :topic/math-academy-id 6375} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561068 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308660 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cded054f-fd7d-5541-b119-acd319ea1369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}(5t)-\\operatorname{sin}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307055}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307055} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebe30a28-0d85-5a80-a24a-88caf298d3fa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308262} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "173c0281-09d3-5067-b83f-37506d1cb0c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-13\\operatorname{sin}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305365}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305365} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdf013e3-bfec-56fb-abcf-075b57f8eb70" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "94b786d3-6c88-5e7c-b171-415f525959f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-334637" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -13 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $\\pm 5\\text{i}.$*\n\n| ${e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\,$ |  | $5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)$ | $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -13 & -1\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 2{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -13{\\alpha }_{1}t & -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues or $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=5\\text{i}t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-5\\text{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(5\\text{i}t) & ={e}^{5\\text{i}t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}\\cdot 5\\text{i}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+5{\\alpha }_{1}\\text{i}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t &=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1} &=\\frac{1}{5t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-13{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-13\\cdot \\frac{1}{5t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =-\\frac{13}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-\\frac{1}{5t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\cdot t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -13\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "26287e9f-9343-5c17-9537-313ae614bd54" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561079}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561075 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308727 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44269325-ce6a-5455-931e-15b7c67f949e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305820}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305820} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f7cd1b4-a3c3-5a92-8505-97219220b6be" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307972} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce17bce7-e09f-50e5-8677-6bf7b0e2a6c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307057}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307057} :answer-field/id #uuid "acadd084-eae4-5cdf-a4f3-de1038487b85" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308073} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce912870-57f5-5b52-93a9-7294f5ae4c37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307060}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307060} :answer-field/id #uuid "d416bd54-772a-557b-b57d-810f93cfad9c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308183} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d01fa5d3-da0e-5ede-9b2c-b888bb92a4be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(1-2t){e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307077}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307077} :answer-field/id #uuid "e717c517-fae6-5429-8329-6a601aec689e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308252}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bf8f7576-f6c0-5d24-9d4e-d8cc050c1036" :question/math-academy-id "q-335093" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t} & t{e}^{-2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-2t}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices $A$ and ${e}^{At}$ above, compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}).$\n\n| $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=A\\,{e}^{At}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}) & =A\\,{e}^{At} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t} & t{e}^{-2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-2t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2{e}^{-2t} & (1-2t){e}^{-2t} \\\\ 0 & -2{e}^{-2t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "5d0f07d8-733c-51e7-9a95-c40bbfc9ff95" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561086}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561079 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561040 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "939d48ec-1c25-5c44-bc01-35fa86ce8bd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560667}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560667} :answer-field/id #uuid "5822d66e-2f18-53dd-b4cd-fb651a40362c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560899} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf58d67f-30ed-5d74-8536-0d89dad1de9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560743}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560743} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c222316-6984-59bf-8c22-0c5cad67de0d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b34e24d7-8981-5c82-b39b-e245e3ef59b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-334730" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The only eigenvalue of $A$ is $2,$ and it has multiplicity two.*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${e}^{At}={e}^{2t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$4t$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-4t$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 4{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -4{\\alpha }_{1}t & 6{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=2t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}r(2t)={e}^{2t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(2t)={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}2t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{2t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n2t{e}^{2t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t}(1-2t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-2{e}^{2t}t+{e}^{2t}(1-2t) \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}(1-4t), \\\\ 6{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =6{e}^{2t}t+{e}^{2t}(1-2t) \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}(1+4t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1-4t & 4t \\\\ -4t & 1+4t\\end{aligned}].\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7c26bff4-82ce-5d40-8919-b6dec6caf103" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561075}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561082 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308655 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36c1c3f8-e34c-5913-9027-40cbf9b38b67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305677}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305677} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6401040-97c5-5632-9c58-3544640ae047" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308054} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40844993-f65c-5c72-af9c-ffdf6d82f4c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305783}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305783} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb369d00-0a03-526e-b8a8-28162f18b93d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308152}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f28e1404-987d-53df-a0ad-e0b6d8de5b42" :question/math-academy-id "q-334630" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $-1\\pm 2\\text{i}.$*\n\n| ${e}^{At}={e}^{-t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 4{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -2{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues or $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=(-1+2\\text{i})t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=(-1-2\\text{i})t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((-1+2\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(-1+2\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(-1+2\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & ={e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)) \\\\ (-{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0})+2{\\alpha }_{1}\\text{i}t & ={e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\,{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2t{\\alpha }_{1} &={e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1} &=\\frac{1}{2t}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2t}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\cdot t+{e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\frac{1}{2t}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\cdot t+{e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "86739e1b-e113-54ad-aa60-4fc9b6a5b447" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561068}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561086 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222006 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c3e688a-d00f-5c7d-bfff-2deb95e138bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10\\operatorname{cos}(10t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306038}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306038} :answer-field/id #uuid "10f8227c-1448-5bfe-9e64-cdcfa325f853" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307576} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c408733a-e25b-5774-baf1-164003c5f78a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-10\\operatorname{cos}(10t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306977}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306977} :answer-field/id #uuid "15ce0198-a457-52fa-a17d-46133d696ab4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307588} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ec9fbd1-bfcf-5774-b8c2-55e9dfa32371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-10\\operatorname{sin}(10t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306368}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306368} :answer-field/id #uuid "e30e1dd1-cc02-52f7-af40-22cd31c5cfdd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308239} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d151806-374d-547d-a63e-b2a3f75a7fe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-10\\operatorname{sin}(10t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306487}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306487} :answer-field/id #uuid "e87e6353-67e7-5e70-80d8-7d8a533a69bf" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ec4ec1fa-f063-5a3c-ba78-66239dbbdec2" :question/math-academy-id "q-335096" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -10 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(10t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(10t)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices $A$ and ${e}^{At}$ above, compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}).$\n\n| $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=A\\,{e}^{At}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}) & =A\\,{e}^{At} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -10 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(10t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(10t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10t) & -10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10t) \\\\ 10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10t) & -10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a9c4980a-13cb-5d93-a06d-edb7046c0908"}] :activity/title "Matrix Exponentials" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560355}]}
